  <data name="HowPresetsWorkText1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A preset is a list of mods to enable along with their preferences. JASM reads and stores mod preferences in the mod&apos;s own .JASM_ModConfig.json file</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HowPresetsWorkText2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>When you create a new preset, JASM generates a list of all enabled mods and their stored preferences. So when you later apply that preset, it will only enable those mods and apply the preferences stored in the preset</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HowPresetsWorkText3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>You can let JASM handle the 3Dmigoto reload by checking the auto-sync checkbox. You can also choose to handle it manually: check the show manual controls checkbox, save/load preferences manually, and refresh 3Dmigoto with the F10 key.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HowPresetsWorkText4" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>You can simply ignore the preset part of this page and use only the manual controls to save mod preferences.</value>
  </data>
